```javascript
const HeavyChart = React.lazy(() => import('./HeavyChart'));

function Dashboard() {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>
      <HeavyChart />
    </Suspense>
  );
}
```

The fallback renders while the dynamic `import()` promise is in flight — that's a code *download*, not a data fetch. Split at route boundaries first (biggest win, users only pay for the route they're on), then at heavy, rarely-used components (modals, charts, rich text editors).

