## Anti-patterns

Memoizing every component (the shallow-compare overhead can outweigh a cheap render), `useMemo` on a value that changes every render anyway, and putting high-frequency state — scroll position, mouse coordinates, keystrokes — into Context.

A function that takes a component and returns a new, enhanced component. Pre-hooks, this was the primary way to share logic (`withRouter`, `connect` from Redux).

```javascript
function withLoading(Component) {
  return function Wrapped({ isLoading, ...props }) {
    if (isLoading) return <Spinner />;
    return <Component {...props} />;
  };
}
const UserListWithLoading = withLoading(UserList);
```

