Use `useTransition` when *you* trigger the state update. Use `useDeferredValue` when you only *receive* a value (a prop) and can't wrap its setter yourself.

```javascript
const deferredQuery = useDeferredValue(query);
const isStale = query !== deferredQuery;
const results = useMemo(() => filter(items, deferredQuery), [items, deferredQuery]);
```

